From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fanasina RANDRIATSARAFARA <m.randriatsarafara.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tee: qseecom: Give the request back when it is INOUT

The request is staged in kernel TZ memory and never copied back. The
Goodix fingerprint application (gfdit) writes its command status into
the request, at offset 28, not into the response: with the downstream
driver the caller sees it because the application works on the caller's
own buffer. Here the status is lost and every command looks like a
silent success.

When the caller passes the request as MEMREF_INOUT, copy the staged
request back after the command, with the patched physical addresses
cleared first so they do not leak to user space.
---
 drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/qseecom/core.c
@@ -974,6 +974,24 @@
 					memcpy(pv, b + off, plen);
 				off += plen;
 			}
+
+			/*
+			 * Some applications write their status back into the
+			 * request rather than the response -- the fingerprint
+			 * application puts it at offset 28 -- relying on the
+			 * downstream driver handing them the caller's own
+			 * buffer. Give that back when the caller asked for it
+			 * with an INOUT request, but scrub the patched
+			 * addresses first: user space has no business with
+			 * physical addresses.
+			 */
+			if ((param[0].attr & TEE_IOCTL_PARAM_ATTR_TYPE_MASK) ==
+			    TEE_IOCTL_PARAM_ATTR_TYPE_MEMREF_INOUT) {
+				for (k = 2; k < arg->num_params; k += 2)
+					memset(b + param[k].u.value.a, 0,
+					       param[k].u.value.b == 4 ? 4 : 8);
+				memcpy(req, b, req_size);
+			}
 		}
 
 out_free:
-- 
